IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc21-nouns`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-19-absolute`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-18`
IMPORT `ccc21-part-19`

-- ccc21-tests-part-19.l4 -- tests for ss 554 to 572 (Part XIX, trial without jury). Expected values written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.
-- Argument order is the GIVEN order of the function under test.

§ `Fixtures`

`s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name` MEANS
    `s 553 the charge` WITH
        `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` IS TRUE
        `s 553 the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS 267, `subsection` IS ""
        `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name`
        `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS 0
        `s 553 how the accused is charged` IS `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
        `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS FALSE

`s 554 test facts: theft of 100 dollars` MEANS
    `s 553 the charge` WITH
        `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` IS TRUE
        `s 553 the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS 334, `subsection` IS ""
        `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS `s 553(a)(i) theft`
        `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS 100
        `s 553 how the accused is charged` IS `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
        `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS FALSE

`s 554 test facts: not charged in an information` MEANS
    `s 553 the charge` WITH
        `s 553 the accused is charged in an information` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the offence charged` IS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS 267, `subsection` IS ""
        `s 553 the offence charged, as paragraph (a) names it` IS `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name`
        `s 553 the theft is theft of cattle` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument` IS FALSE
        `s 553 the alleged value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS 0
        `s 553 how the accused is charged` IS `s 553(b) with the offence itself`
        `s 553 the offence is under paragraph 4(4)(a) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS FALSE

GIVEN class IS A `Class of offence`
      mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      imprisonment IS AN Imprisonment
      facts IS A `s 553 the charge`
GIVETH A `s 535 the charge`
`s 554 test charge` MEANS
    `s 535 the charge` WITH
        `s 535 the class of the offence charged` IS class
        `s 535 the mode in which the prosecutor proceeds` IS mode
        `s 535 the maximum imprisonment for the offence on indictment` IS imprisonment
        `s 535 the facts that bear on absolute jurisdiction` IS facts

-- A: indictable, ten years, not absolute. B: summary only. C: indictable, ten years, absolute (theft of 100 dollars). D: indictable, ten years, not charged in an information.
-- E: hybrid, prosecuted by indictment. F: hybrid, prosecuted summarily. G: indictable, five years. H: indictable, five years less a day. I: indictable, five years and a day. J: indictable, life. K: indictable, no maximum stated.
`s 554 test charge A` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge B` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` `on summary conviction` (`imprisonment for a term of` `six months`) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge C` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 554 test facts: theft of 100 dollars`
`s 554 test charge D` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 554 test facts: not charged in an information`
`s 554 test charge E` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge F` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` `on summary conviction` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge G` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge H` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, TRUE)) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge I` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 1, FALSE)) `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge J` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` `imprisonment for life` `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`
`s 554 test charge K` MEANS `s 554 test charge` `an indictable offence` `by indictment` `no imprisonment is stated` `s 554 test facts: an offence section 553 does not name`

`s 554 test PCJ` MEANS `s 536(2) trial by a provincial court judge`
`s 554 test judge` MEANS `s 536(2) trial by a judge without a jury`
`s 554 test jury` MEANS `s 536(2) trial by a court composed of a judge and jury`
`s 554 test elects PCJ` MEANS `s 536(2) elects` `s 554 test PCJ`
`s 554 test elects judge` MEANS `s 536(2) elects` `s 554 test judge`
`s 554 test elects jury` MEANS `s 536(2) elects` `s 554 test jury`

GIVEN elected IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
      wish IS A `s 536(2) mode of trial`
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      requested IS A BOOLEAN
      completed IS A MAYBE DATE
      reelection IS A DATE
      trial IS A DATE
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 561 the re-election facts`
`s 561 test facts` MEANS
    `s 561 the re-election facts` WITH
        `s 561 the mode elected or deemed elected` IS elected
        `s 561 the mode the accused wishes to re-elect` IS wish
        `s 561 the accused is entitled to request a preliminary inquiry` IS entitled
        `s 561 a preliminary inquiry has been requested under subsection 536(4)` IS requested
        `s 561 the date the preliminary inquiry was completed` IS completed
        `s 561 the date of the re-election` IS reelection
        `s 561 the day first appointed for the trial` IS trial
        `s 561 the prosecutor has consented in writing` IS consent

-- Days are counted from 1 January 2026: 1 March 2026 is 59 days later, 2 March 2026 is 60 days later and 3 March 2026 is 61 days later (January has 31 days and February 2026 has 28).
`s 561 test day 0` MEANS Date 1 1 2026
`s 561 test day 59` MEANS Date 1 3 2026
`s 561 test day 60` MEANS Date 2 3 2026
`s 561 test day 61` MEANS Date 3 3 2026

GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`s 557 test provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS sec, `subsection` IS sub

§ `Tests -- section 554`

-- 554(1): indictable, not 469, not absolute, elects a provincial court judge, not Nunavut: JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` NOTHING `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the offence is mentioned in section 469 is for that section
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST TRUE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "other than an offence that is mentioned in section 469": outside the limit of a grant
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsection (2)": Nunavut
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if the accused elects to be tried by a provincial court judge"
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects jury` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 536(2) does not elect` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge B` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- summary conviction only: not "an indictable offence"
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge C` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- absolute jurisdiction under section 553
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge D` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "charged in an information"
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge E` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- hybrid, prosecuted by indictment (NOTES.md F4)
#ASSERT `s 554(1) a provincial court judge may try the accused` `s 554 test charge F` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- hybrid, prosecuted summarily

-- 554(2): Nunavut, elects a judge without a jury
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "With respect to criminal proceedings in Nunavut"
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects PCJ` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if the accused elects to be tried by a judge without a jury"
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects jury` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST TRUE) `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 469
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge A` NOTHING `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge B` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- summary conviction only
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge C` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- absolute jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 554(2) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may try the accused` `s 554 test charge D` (JUST FALSE) `s 554 test elects judge` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not charged in an information

§ `Tests -- sections 555 and 555.1`

-- 555(1): before the provincial court judge, it appears the charge should be prosecuted by indictment, before a defence is entered
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "at any time before the accused has entered a defence" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge may decide not to adjudicate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "If in any proceedings under this Part an accused is before a provincial court judge"
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "it appears to the provincial court judge that for any reason the charge should be prosecuted by indictment"
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge may decide not to adjudicate` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge shall inform the accused of the decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(1) the provincial court judge shall inform the accused of the decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "decide not to adjudicate and shall then inform"
#ASSERT `s 555(1.1) the words in which the provincial court judge puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or you may elect to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you are entitled to one and you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"
#ASSERT `s 555(1.1) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (1.1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(1.1) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (1.1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "If the provincial court judge has decided not to adjudicate"
#ASSERT `s 555(1.2) the provincial court judge shall continue the proceedings as a preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(1.2) the provincial court judge shall continue the proceedings as a preliminary inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither the accused nor the prosecutor requests one
#ASSERT `s 555(1.2) the provincial court judge shall continue the proceedings as a preliminary inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not entitled

-- 555(2): theft (paragraph 553(a)) prosecuted by indictment, evidence before adjudication shows a will or a value over 5,000 dollars
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(i) theft` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` FALSE `s 553(a)(i) theft` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "If an accused is before a provincial court judge"
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an offence mentioned in paragraph 553(a)
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(i) theft` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not prosecuted by indictment
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(i) theft` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "at any time before the provincial court judge makes an adjudication": already made
#ASSERT `s 555(2) the provincial court judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(i) theft` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the evidence does not establish a will or a value over 5,000 dollars

-- 555(3): the record of the election
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(a) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election` TRUE `s 554 test elects judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(a) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election` TRUE `s 554 test elects jury` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(a) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election` TRUE `s 536(2) does not elect` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or does not elect when put to their election"
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(a) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election` TRUE `s 554 test elects PCJ` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- that is paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(a) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election` FALSE `s 554 test elects judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not put to their election
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election and continue with the trial` TRUE `s 554 test elects PCJ` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election and continue with the trial` TRUE `s 554 test elects judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555(3)(b) the provincial court judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election and continue with the trial` FALSE `s 554 test elects PCJ` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 555.1: the Nunavut counterpart
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "at any time before the accused has entered a defence"
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may decide not to adjudicate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice may decide not to adjudicate` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge shall inform the accused of the decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1) the judge shall inform the accused of the decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1.1) the words in which the judge puts the accused to an election` EQUALS "You have the option to elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you do not elect now, you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury. If you elect to be tried by a judge without a jury or by a court composed of a judge and jury or if you are deemed to have elected to be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury, you will have a preliminary inquiry only if you are entitled to one and you or the prosecutor requests one. How do you elect to be tried?"
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1.1) the judge shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (1.1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1.1) the judge shall put the accused to an election in the words of subsection (1.1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1.2) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election or deemed election and continue the proceedings as a preliminary inquiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(1.2) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the election or deemed election and continue the proceedings as a preliminary inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` FALSE `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a) an offence that paragraph (a) does not name` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(2) the judge shall put the accused to their election in accordance with subsection 536.1(2.1)` TRUE `s 553(a)(ii) obtaining money or property by false pretences` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(3) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election and continue with the trial` TRUE `s 554 test elects judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(3) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election and continue with the trial` TRUE `s 536(2) does not elect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(3) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election and continue with the trial` TRUE `s 554 test elects PCJ` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the paragraph names only a judge without a jury, a jury, or no election
#ASSERT `s 555.1(3) the judge shall endorse on the information a record of the nature of the election or deemed election and continue with the trial` FALSE `s 554 test elects judge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(4) this section, and not section 555, applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 555.1(4) this section, and not section 555, applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "in respect of criminal proceedings in Nunavut"

§ `Tests -- sections 556 to 559`

-- 556(1): an accused organization shall appear by counsel or agent
#ASSERT `s 556(1) the accused organization shall appear by counsel or agent` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 556(1) the accused organization shall appear by counsel or agent` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- an individual: the subsection speaks only of "An accused organization"
#ASSERT `s 556(1) the accused organization shall appear by counsel or agent` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the accused is an organization is for section 2

-- 556(2): an organization that does not appear
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(a) the judge may proceed with the trial of the charge in the absence of the accused organization` TRUE (`s 554 test charge C`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- absolute jurisdiction (theft of 100 dollars)
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(a) the judge may proceed with the trial of the charge in the absence of the accused organization` TRUE (`s 554 test charge A`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an offence over which the judge has absolute jurisdiction: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(a) the judge may proceed with the trial of the charge in the absence of the accused organization` FALSE (`s 554 test charge C`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where an accused organization does not appear pursuant to a summons and service of the summons on the organization is proved" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(b) the judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the accused organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE (`s 554 test charge A`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(b) the judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the accused organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE (`s 554 test charge C`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if the charge is not one over which the judge has absolute jurisdiction"
#ASSERT `s 556(2)(b) the judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the accused organization must appear in the trial court` FALSE (`s 554 test charge A`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 556(3) the provincial court judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 556(3) the provincial court judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a preliminary inquiry is requested under subsection 536(4)
#ASSERT `s 556(3) the provincial court judge shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the organization does not appear
#ASSERT `s 556(4) the justice of the peace or the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 556(4) the justice of the peace or the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 556(4) the justice of the peace or the judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice shall fix the date for the trial or the date on which the organization must appear in the trial court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- 557: the evidence is taken in accordance with Part XVIII (ss 535 to 551), other than subsections 540(7) to (9)
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(6)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(7)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than subsections 540(7) to (9)"
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(8)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(9)") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 535 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section of Part XVIII
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 551 "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section of Part XVIII
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 534 "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in Part XVIII
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` TRUE (`s 557 test provision` 552 "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in Part XVIII
#ASSERT `s 557 the evidence of witnesses must be taken in accordance with the provision of Part XVIII` FALSE (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(1)") EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not tried in accordance with this Part

-- 558: tried by a judge without a jury
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge B` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an indictable offence
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- an offence mentioned in section 469
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- did not elect or re-elect a judge without a jury
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge A` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 469 is for that section
#ASSERT `s 558 the accused shall be tried by a judge without a jury` `s 554 test charge A` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "subject to this Part": another provision displaces the election

-- 559: a court of record; the record is kept
#ASSERT `s 559(1) the judge is a court of record for all purposes of the trial and proceedings connected with it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 559(1) the judge is a court of record for all purposes of the trial and proceedings connected with it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "A judge who holds a trial under this Part"
#ASSERT `s 559(2) the record of the trial shall be kept in the court over which the judge presides` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 559(2) the record of the trial shall be kept in the court over which the judge presides` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 560`

#ASSERT `s 560(1) a judge having jurisdiction shall fix a time and place for the trial of the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) the sheriff's written notice
#ASSERT `s 560(1) a judge having jurisdiction shall fix a time and place for the trial of the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) the clerk's notice
#ASSERT `s 560(1) a judge having jurisdiction shall fix a time and place for the trial of the accused` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither notice received
#ASSERT `s 560(1) a judge having jurisdiction shall fix a time and place for the trial of the accused` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the accused did not elect a judge without a jury
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the sheriff or other person having custody of the accused shall give the notice mentioned in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the sheriff or other person having custody of the accused shall give the notice mentioned in paragraph (1)(a)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the notice is given within twenty-four hours after the accused is ordered to stand trial` 24 EQUALS TRUE   -- the 24th hour (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the notice is given within twenty-four hours after the accused is ordered to stand trial` 23 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the notice is given within twenty-four hours after the accused is ordered to stand trial` 24.5 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(2) the notice is given within twenty-four hours after the accused is ordered to stand trial` 25 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(a) the accused shall be notified forthwith by the sheriff or other person having custody of the time and place fixed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(a) the accused shall be notified forthwith by the sheriff or other person having custody of the time and place fixed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in custody
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(a) the accused shall be notified forthwith by the sheriff or other person having custody of the time and place fixed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(b) the accused shall be produced at the time and place fixed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(b) the accused shall be produced at the time and place fixed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(3)(b) the accused shall be produced at the time and place fixed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(4) the duty of ascertaining from the clerk of the court the time and place fixed for the trial is on the accused` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- not in custody
#ASSERT `s 560(4) the duty of ascertaining from the clerk of the court the time and place fixed for the trial is on the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Where an accused is not in custody"
#ASSERT `s 560(4) the accused shall attend for their trial at the time and place fixed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 560(4) the accused shall attend for their trial at the time and place fixed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 560(5) repealed` EQUALS "(5) [Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 109]"

§ `Tests -- section 561 (right to re-elect)`

-- Arguments of `s 561 test facts`: mode elected, mode wished, entitled to request a preliminary inquiry, requested one under 536(4), date completed (MAYBE), date of the re-election, day first appointed for the trial, written consent.

-- 561(1)(a)(i): a preliminary inquiry was requested; with the prosecutor's written consent, to be tried by a provincial court judge, at any time before or after completion
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 59` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- before completion
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- "with the written consent of the prosecutor" not given: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "to be tried by a provincial court judge"
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no preliminary inquiry was requested: paragraph (a) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(i) the accused may re-elect to be tried by a provincial court judge, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- already elected a provincial court judge: subsection (1) is for another mode

-- 561(1)(a)(ii): as of right, before completion or before the 60th day following completion, another mode other than a provincial court judge
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 59` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the 59th day after completion: before the 60th
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 60` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the 60th day after completion (listed: where/when/upon group, a stated period)
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 61` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the 61st day
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the inquiry is not yet completed
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of completion itself
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a provincial court judge is the mode excluded
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test judge` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the same mode is not "another mode"
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no preliminary inquiry requested: paragraph (b) governs
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(ii) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- elected a provincial court judge: subsection (2) governs

-- 561(1)(a)(iii): on or after the 60th day following completion, any mode, with consent
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 60` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the 60th day after completion (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 59` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the 59th day: not yet "on or after the 60th day" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 61` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no written consent: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 61` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the inquiry has not been completed, so no 60th day has been reached
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(a)(iii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 61` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no preliminary inquiry requested

-- 561(1)(b): no preliminary inquiry requested, or not entitled to one
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly 60 days before the day first appointed (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 59 days before: "not later than 60 days before" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 61 days before
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- not entitled to a preliminary inquiry
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- entitled and requested one: paragraph (a) governs
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a provincial court judge is the mode excluded
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(i) the accused may re-elect another mode of trial other than trial by a provincial court judge, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test judge` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the same mode
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(ii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(ii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no written consent
#ASSERT `s 561(1)(b)(ii) the accused may re-elect any mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- entitled and requested one: paragraph (a) governs

-- 561(1) taken whole: the footing
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 as of right`   -- (a)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 as of right`   -- (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test PCJ` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`   -- (a)(i)
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 60` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`   -- (a)(iii)
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`   -- (b)(ii), too late for (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no paragraph gives the right on these facts
#ASSERT `s 561(1) the basis on which the accused who elected or is deemed to have elected may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test jury` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- elected a provincial court judge: subsection (2), not (1)

-- 561(2): an accused who elects a provincial court judge
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 60 days before (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 59 days before (listed: where/when/upon group, a stated period)
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- did not elect a provincial court judge: subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test PCJ` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- another mode
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "after that time with the written consent"
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no written consent
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not yet "after that time" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the accused who elects to be tried by a provincial court judge may re-elect another mode of trial after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- did not elect a provincial court judge
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the basis on which the accused who elected a provincial court judge may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 as of right`
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the basis on which the accused who elected a provincial court judge may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`
#ASSERT `s 561(2) the basis on which the accused who elected a provincial court judge may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test PCJ` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- the seam other parts ask: did the accused re-elect?
#ASSERT `s 561 the accused re-elected` TRUE (JUST `s 561 as of right`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561 the accused re-elected` FALSE (JUST `s 561 as of right`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561 the accused re-elected` TRUE (JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561 the accused re-elected` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 561 gives no footing for the re-election on these facts
#ASSERT `s 561 the accused re-elected` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no re-election is a plain fact

-- 561(3) to (7): notices, notifications and attendance
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give notice in writing of their intention to re-elect to the justice presiding at the preliminary inquiry` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give notice in writing of their intention to re-elect to the justice presiding at the preliminary inquiry` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give with the notice the written consent of the prosecutor` TRUE (JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "if that consent is required"
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give with the notice the written consent of the prosecutor` TRUE (JUST `s 561 as of right`) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- consent is not required
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give with the notice the written consent of the prosecutor` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 561(3) the accused shall give with the notice the written consent of the prosecutor` FALSE (JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(3)(a) the justice shall put the accused to their re-election in the manner set out in subsection (7)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(3)(a) the justice shall put the accused to their re-election in the manner set out in subsection (7)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(3)(b) the justice shall notify a provincial court judge or clerk of the court and send the documents` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(3)(b) the justice shall notify a provincial court judge or clerk of the court and send the documents` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the justice is a provincial court judge
#ASSERT `s 561(3)(b) the justice shall notify a provincial court judge or clerk of the court and send the documents` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(4) the accused shall give notice in writing to the provincial court judge before whom the accused appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(4) the accused shall give notice in writing to the provincial court judge before whom the accused appeared and pleaded or to a clerk of the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(5) the accused shall give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court of the accused's original election` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(5) the accused shall give notice in writing to a judge or clerk of the court of the accused's original election` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(5) the judge or clerk shall notify the judge or clerk of the court by which the accused wishes to be tried and send the documents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(5) the judge or clerk shall notify the judge or clerk of the court by which the accused wishes to be tried and send the documents` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(6) the provincial court judge or judge shall forthwith appoint a time and place for the accused to re-elect and cause notice to be given to the accused and the prosecutor` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(6) the provincial court judge or judge shall forthwith appoint a time and place for the accused to re-elect and cause notice to be given to the accused and the prosecutor` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall attend at the time and place appointed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall attend at the time and place appointed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall, if in custody, be produced at the time and place appointed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall, if in custody, be produced at the time and place appointed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in custody: nothing to produce
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall, if in custody, be produced at the time and place appointed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall be put to a re-election` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall be put to a re-election` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the charge, indictment or information has not been read
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the accused shall be put to a re-election` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 561(7) the words in which the accused is put to their re-election` EQUALS "You have given notice of your intention to re-elect the mode of your trial. You now have the option to do so. How do you intend to re-elect?"

§ `Tests -- section 561.1 (Nunavut)`

-- 561.1(1): any other mode, with the prosecutor's written consent, at any time
#ASSERT `s 561.1(1) the accused may re-elect any other mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 561.1(1) the accused may re-elect any other mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no written consent: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 561.1(1) the accused may re-elect any other mode of trial, with the written consent of the prosecutor` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test judge` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "any other mode"

-- 561.1(2): not requested a preliminary inquiry, or not entitled: as of right up to 60 days before the day first appointed
#ASSERT `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 60` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 60 days before (boundary)
#ASSERT `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 59 days before (listed: where/when/upon group, a stated period)
#ASSERT `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` FALSE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- not entitled
#ASSERT `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- entitled and requested one: subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 561.1(2) the accused may re-elect to be tried by any other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test judge` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "any other mode"

-- 561.1(3): requested a preliminary inquiry: as of right before completion or before the 60th day after it
#ASSERT `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 59` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the 59th day after completion
#ASSERT `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE (JUST `s 561 test day 0`) `s 561 test day 60` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the 60th day after completion (listed: where/when/upon group, a stated period)
#ASSERT `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the inquiry is not yet completed
#ASSERT `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no request under 536.1(3): subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 561.1(3) the accused may re-elect to be tried by the other mode of trial, as of right` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test judge` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "the other mode"
#ASSERT `s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 as of right`   -- (2)
#ASSERT `s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 61` FALSE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 as of right`   -- (3)
#ASSERT `s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` TRUE) EQUALS JUST `s 561 only with the written consent of the prosecutor`   -- (1), too late for (2)
#ASSERT `s 561.1 the basis on which the accused may re-elect` (`s 561 test facts` `s 554 test jury` `s 554 test judge` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `s 561 test day 0` `s 561 test day 59` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

