#ASSERT `s 570(2) a certified copy of the order shall be drawn up and delivered to the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 570(3)
#ASSERT `s 570(3) the provincial court judge shall transmit the written charge, the memorandum of adjudication and the conviction, if any, into the custody the Attorney General directs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 570(3) the provincial court judge shall transmit the written charge, the memorandum of adjudication and the conviction, if any, into the custody the Attorney General directs` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 570(4): sufficient evidence (is a copy of Form 35, 36 or 37, certified or proved a true copy, identity proved)
#ASSERT `s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "on proof of the identity of the person to whom the conviction or order relates"
#ASSERT `s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not certified and not proved a true copy: the subsection says nothing of it
#ASSERT `s 570(4) the copy is sufficient evidence in any legal proceedings to prove the conviction, the making of the order or the acquittal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a copy of a conviction in Form 35 or an order in Form 36 or 37
-- 570(5): (the seam: the accused is an organization; the accused is convicted)
#ASSERT `s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than an organization"
#ASSERT `s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not convicted
#ASSERT `s 570(5) the judge or provincial court judge shall issue a warrant of committal in Form 21` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 2 decides who is an organization
#ASSERT `s 570(5) section 528 applies in respect of the warrant of committal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 570(5) section 528 applies in respect of the warrant of committal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "issued under this subsection"
-- 570(6)
#ASSERT `s 570(6) a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 570(6) a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the copy is not certified by the clerk
#ASSERT `s 570(6) a copy of the warrant of committal, certified by the clerk, is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the warrant was not signed by a clerk
-- 571
#ASSERT `s 571(1) a judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may adjourn a trial from time to time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 571(1) a judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may adjourn a trial from time to time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until it is finally terminated" (listed: where/when/upon group)
#ASSERT `s 571(1) a judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part may adjourn a trial from time to time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "A judge or provincial court judge acting under this Part"
#ASSERT `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if information related to the victim's interests is readily available": it is not
#ASSERT `s 571(2) the judge or provincial court judge shall consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 572: (the provision, the proceedings are under this Part, the provision is inconsistent with this Part, the Part XVIII provision relates to transmission of the record)
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 493 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section of Part XVI
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 529.5 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section of Part XVI
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 530 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Part XVII is not in the list
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 574 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section of Part XX
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 672 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section of Part XX
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 672.1 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Part XX.1 is not in the list
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 716 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section of Part XXIII
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 751.1 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section of Part XXIII
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 752 "") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Part XXIV is not in the list
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 551 "") TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- Part XVIII, the transmission of the record
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 540 "(1)") TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- Part XVIII, not the transmission limb
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 600 "") TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- Part XX but inconsistent: "in so far as they are not inconsistent with this Part"
#ASSERT `s 572 the provision applies to the proceedings under this Part` (`s 557 test provision` 600 "") FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not proceedings under this Part

§ `Tests -- the regulative rules of sections 565(3) and 570(1), run as traces`

-- 565(3): the accused gives the notice, then the judge passes it on. Expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 565(3) the accused must give notice and the judge or clerk must pass it on` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 565(3) gives notice in writing of the intention to re-elect to a judge or clerk of the court where the indictment has been filed or preferred` AT 1
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 565(3) notifies a judge having jurisdiction or clerk of the court by which the accused wishes to be tried and sends the documents` AT 2

-- 565(3): the accused gives the notice and nobody passes it on. Expected: not fulfilled (the judge's obligation remains)
#TRACE `s 565(3) the accused must give notice and the judge or clerk must pass it on` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 565(3) gives notice in writing of the intention to re-elect to a judge or clerk of the court where the indictment has been filed or preferred` AT 1

-- 570(1): the judge endorses the information, then sentences. Expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 570(1) the judge must endorse the information and then sentence the accused` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 570(1) endorses the information accordingly` AT 1
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 570(1) sentences the accused or otherwise deals with the accused in the manner authorized by law` AT 2
